  "reasoning": "The patient presents with stiffness and weakness in the neck muscles, noticeable joint swelling ('joints have grown'), and significant difficulty walking due to stiffness and discomfort. These symptoms collectively indicate an inflammatory musculoskeletal condition. While cervical spondylosis could explain neck stiffness, it does not account for generalized joint swelling and ambulation issues. The combination of swollen joints, widespread stiffness, and mobility impairment is classic for arthritis, which best explains all the presented symptoms together.",
